  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_06. Let triangle MNO be a triangle with sides MN = 10, NO = 14, MO = 12. Let triangle PQR be a triangle with sides QR = 21, PR = 18. Triangle MNO is similar to triangle PQR by AA similarity with scale factor 1.5. Find the length of PQ in PQR.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A surveyor is comparing two triangular plots of land. The original plot MNO has sides MN = 10 meters, NO = 14 meters, and MO = 12 meters. A developer wants to create a larger similar plot PQR for a new project.\n\nThe surveyor confirms that triangle MNO is similar to triangle PQR by AA similarity, with a scale factor of 1.5. This means each side of PQR is 1.5 times the corresponding side in MNO.\n\nThe surveyor has already measured two sides of the new plot: QR = 21 meters and PR = 18 meters. Before finalizing the land purchase, she needs to determine the third side of the plot.\n\nWhat is the length of PQ?"
}